LinkedIn Learning is an excellent resource that I haven’t explored prior to this assignment.  As mentioned, there are many soft skill pathways that can benefit any professional.  The platform has a really unique built in AI tool as well.  I utilized this feature to build a custom pathway, with the goal of transitioning to a career in software development.  The guide consisted of 3 main topics, with courses applicable to each:

Foundations of Software Engineering:


- Learning Python
- Programming Foundations: Fundamentals
- Agile Software Development
- Problem Solving and Version Control
- Python Data Structures and Algorithms
- Advanced Algorithmic Thinking with Python
- Programing Foundations: Version Control with Git
- Communication and Career Transition


Tech Career Skills: Effective Technical Communication


- Effective Career Change Strategies for Young Professionals
- Building a Diverse Professional Network
- Building Core Software Development Skills


Programming Foundations: Software Testing/QA


Agile Software Development
Python Object-Oriented Programming

I am surprised by how comprehensive the courses that the pathway tool chose, with a nice balance of emphasis on both soft and technical skills that may be helpful in an interview process.  Some of the course material seems very familiar and may serve as more of a refresher for topics that were covered in depth as a student, while others appear to be more industry specific and may have been missed or glossed over in a more formal educational setting. 

I chose to explore the Python Data Structures and Algorithms course in more depth.  Again, the quality of the course was surprising.  The platform goes beyond video learning and includes source files that can be downloaded and a built in programming tool for coding exercises.  I completed around half of the course and am finding it to be a very valuable resource.  Leetcode does not come easy, and this has been a great set of training wheels as I seek a successful career transition within the next year or two.  My greatest takeaway is that Python will serve as an excellent language to use during technical interviews, and seems to be widely accepted by employers.  

I find tools like LinkedIn Learning to be excellent foundations for the deeper exploration that will be required in order to achieve a successful career change. A focus on both technical and soft skills are critical, and this platform brings attention to both.  With access through the University, this is a tool that I plan to use to revisit important topics well after graduation. 
